# Atlas Engineering Knowledge Base (EKB) — Implementation Plan

> **This is NOT documentation. This is the project's constitution.**
> Every implementation decision traces back to the EKB.
> Every architectural change requires an EKB update.
> The EKB is a living engineering reference, not a static document set.

---

## Goal

Produce the **Atlas Engineering Knowledge Base** — a complete, production-grade, enterprise-quality engineering reference for a local-first, multi-agent AI Software Engineering Platform. The EKB will live in `c:\Users\psbon\CodeGuru\docs\` and serve as the authoritative foundation for the entire project lifecycle.

No production code will be written. Every file is Markdown with Mermaid diagrams where they improve clarity.

---

## Locked Decisions

| Dimension | Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| **Output location** | `c:\Users\psbon\CodeGuru\docs\` | User workspace |
| **Format** | Markdown (`.md`) with Mermaid | Version-controllable, portable |
| **AI Models (fixed)** | Qwen3-Coder, DeepSeek R1, BAAI BGE-M3 | User constraint |
| **Core orchestration** | Rust | Performance, safety, concurrency |
| **AI runtime & agents** | Python | LLM ecosystem compatibility |
| **Desktop shell** | Tauri | Lightweight, cross-platform, Rust-native |
| **Frontend** | React + TypeScript | Ecosystem, type safety |
| **Primary database** | PostgreSQL (prod) / SQLite (local) | Reliability + lightweight option |
| **Vector database** | Qdrant | Local-first, performant, Rust-native |
| **Repository parsing** | Tree-sitter | Industry standard, multi-language |
| **Messaging** | NATS (abstractable) | Start in-process, scale to distributed |
| **Inference** | Ollama (dev), adapters for llama.cpp/vLLM | Flexibility |
| **Containerization** | Docker | Standard |
| **Observability** | OpenTelemetry | Vendor-neutral standard |

